<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Æscwine of Essex</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">527 (traditional)</span> · Also known as Aescwine of Essex</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Æscwine is the traditional founder of the East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> royal line, placed by later sources in 527. Nothing certain is known of him, but the genealogies of the kings of Essex begin with him, and most of his descendants bore names beginning with S.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aescwine-of-essex.jpg" alt="Æscwine of Essex" width="320" height="312" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Speed · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erkenwin_-_John_Speed.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
